  "summary": "The Instron 5967 universal testing machine (EQ15) is directly suited for uniaxial compression testing to determine the compressive modulus of your bovine trabecular bone specimens. You will need to confirm the availability of flat compression platens, a load cell sized appropriately for the specimen cross-section, and a fluid bath if testing in hydrated conditions. If you also need to correlate mechanical stiffness with trabecular architecture or porosity, micro-CT would be the standard technique, but it is not available among the listed instruments."
